  "goodToKnow": "Das Platin is platinum: ein Platinring, Platin-Schmuck. It's used in catalytic converters (Katalysatoren), jewellery and investment. In music, Platin means a platinum award; in Germany, an album goes platinum at 200,000 units. Stressed on the first syllable: PLAA-tin. The name comes from Spanish platina (little silver). Like most metals, it's neuter: das Gold, das Silber, das Platin. It has no plural."
